From d3b1cc114ff484f8cfbfcd6ac7e4bf6835715879 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 01:45:21 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 253/294] wip: capture a Vulkan compute draw and replay it from
 the native driver

The reference now has a compute-based triangle draw (vktq_draw + tri.comp: a compute shader rasterises a
512x512 triangle, self-verified: inside=73728, outside=188416, bad=0), and its CDM job is captured with
dump hooks for the compute fw stream, control stream, context state BO, static context state, PDS
programs, USC programs, descriptor-set constants and the descriptor set itself.

The native probe gets a compute-draw replay (PVR_PROBE_CDM_DIR): it creates a compute context from the
captured static state, reconstructs every buffer the captured job points at at the same device addresses
(control stream, context state, border table, PDS kernel/fence/descriptor programs, USC programs,
descriptor page with the target's pco buffer descriptor, and the target), submits the captured fw stream
through a new pvr_job_submit_compute_sync(), and reads the target back looking for the triangle.

Status: the submit is accepted and the firmware kicks DM4/CDM, but the job hangs the GPU (the firmware
reports an HWR and sends an unhandled context-reset FWCCB notification); the target reads back all zero.
Everything the job references is reconstructed, so the missing piece is in the reconstructed state (CDM
context state / CSW programs / descriptor constants), not the submission plumbing. Captures are in
open-driver-perf/captures/cdm/.
